-- F02: template-level observer exposure.
--
-- This package is a security fixture. The defect below is deliberate. Do not fix
-- it: the oracle in the sibling test package asserts that the defect is still
-- present, so repairing the template makes the fixture fail by design.
--
-- Intended disclosure policy
--   A CompensationRecord states what an employer pays an employee. The employee and
--   the employer are parties to it. A payroll vendor processes the payment run, so it
--   is named on the contract, but the vendor is engaged only to move an already
--   agreed amount: it has no business need to read the salary or the review notes.
--
-- The defect
--   `vendor` is declared as a template-level `observer`. Observer status in Daml is
--   whole-contract, not per-field, so naming the vendor as an observer discloses
--   every field of the contract to it, including `annualSalary` and `reviewNotes`.
--
-- Scope of the claim
--   This is a TEMPLATE-LEVEL OBSERVER EXPOSURE defect: the stakeholder set written
--   into the template is wider than the disclosure policy requires. It is not a
--   claim about explicit contract disclosure (the off-ledger `disclose` mechanism,
--   which grants read rights at submission time), and it is not a claim about
--   Canton-network privacy or about what any particular participant node stores.
module Payroll where

template CompensationRecord
  with
    employer : Party
    employee : Party
    vendor : Party
    annualSalary : Decimal
    reviewNotes : Text
  where
    signatory employer
    -- The employee is a legitimate stakeholder. The vendor should not be one: it
    -- needs a payment instruction, not the compensation record. This single word is
    -- the vulnerability.
    observer employee, vendor

-- The disclosure the vendor legitimately needs: who to pay, and how much to move
-- for this run. It deliberately does not carry the salary or the review notes.
template PaymentInstruction
  with
    employer : Party
    employee : Party
    vendor : Party
    amount : Decimal
  where
    signatory employer
    observer vendor
